# glibc239-libm verification (tools/glibc239_libm_proof/harness.rs), 2026-11-02.
# Reference: the process libm.  First block: inside docker ubuntu:24.04, whose libc6 is glibc 2.39 (the
# references' C library), on an x86-64 CPU with FMA and AVX2, so glibc's ifunc picks the FMA variants the port
# transcribes.  Second block: the same binary and seeds on the host's glibc 2.44, which reduces huge sin, cos and
# tan arguments differently from 2.39; the port gives 2.39's word on every one of those (first block, same seed).
# Indented lines are the first 20 mismatches of a run, printed before its summary line; 'port' is
# glibc239-libm, 'libm' the process libm. The binary32 lines grade rw-libm's expf, logf and powf.

